178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Indian cosmetics industry has rapidly expanded, yet a significant gap remains in shade inclusivity. Most international and domestic brands often cater disproportionately to lighter skin tones, leaving individuals with medium to deeper complexions underserved. This lack of inclusivity not only limits consumer choice but also reinforces colorism in beauty standards.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Moreover, AI-powered beauty apps and recommendation engines frequently misclassify Indian skin tones due to biased datasets trained primarily on Western complexion ranges. This results in inaccurate product suggestions and poor consumer trust.Therefore, there is a critical need for a data-driven approach that evaluates shade ranges across brands.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
